{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me work through this task carefully. There's a frozen ranking rule from RANKING_RULE.md. I'll apply it to the six guides.\n\nFirst, let me understand the data.\n\n**candidates.csv**\n| guide_id | spacer | activity_score | coding_bystander_count |\n|----------|--------|----------------|------------------------|\n| g01 | GACTGACCTGAACTGACCAA | 0.82 | 1 |\n| g02 | CTGACTGACCAAGTTCAGGA | 0.67 | 0 |\n| g03 | TTCAGGACTGACCTGACTGA | 0.74 | 0 |\n| g04 | AGGCTGACTAACCTGACCTG | 0.59 | 0 |\n| g05 | CCTGAACTGACCTGACTGGA | 0.78 | 2 |\n| g06 | GAACTGACCTGACTGGACCA | 0.64 | 0 |\n\n**off_targets.csv**\n| guide_id | locus | mismatches | region | expression_risk |\n|----------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------------|\n| g01 | chr2:100120-100139 | 1 | coding_exon | high |\n| g02 | chr5:220010-220029 | 3 | intron | low |\n| g03 | chr7:330040-330059 | 2 | coding_exon | medium |\n| g04 | chr9:440070-440089 | 4 | intergenic | low |\n| g05 | chr12:550100-550119 | 1 | coding_exon | high |\n| g06 | chr14:660130-660149 | 3 | intergenic | low |\n\nNow let me apply the rule.\n\n**Rule 1: Rejection conditions**\n- There's an annotated off-target on a coding exon with 2 or fewer mismatches, OR\n- expression_risk = high, OR\n- coding_bystander_count > 0\n\nCheck each guide:\n\n**g01**:\n- Off-target: coding_exon, 1 mismatch (2 or fewer → yes), expression_risk = high\n- coding_bystander_count = 1 > 0\n- → Reject (all three conditions triggered)\n\n**g02**:\n- Off-target: intron, 3 mismatches, low\n- coding_bystander_count = 0\n- Not on a coding exon, expression_risk is not high, bystanders is 0\n- → Not rejected\n\n**g03**:\n- Off-target: coding_exon, 2 mismatches (2 or fewer → yes), expression_risk = medium\n- coding_bystander_count = 0\n- → Reject (coding exon with 2 or fewer mismatches)\n\n**g04**:\n- Off-target: intergenic, 4 mismatches, low\n- coding_bystander_count = 0\n- → Not rejected\n\n**g05**:\n- Off-target: coding_exon, 1 mismatch (2 or fewer → yes), expression_risk = high\n- coding_bystander_count = 2 > 0\n- → Reject (all three conditions triggered)\n\n**g06**:\n- Off-target: intergenic, 3 mismatches, low\n- coding_bystander_count = 0\n- → Not rejected\n\nTherefore non-rejected: g02, g04, g06\nRejected: g01, g03, g05\n\n**Rule 2: Risk classes**\n\nFor non-rejected guides:\n- g02: no coding exon hits, no high-expression hits, bystanders is 0.\n  - critical? High-expression hit? No. Bystanders ≥ 2? No. Coding exon hit with 1 mismatch? No. → Not critical.\n  - high? Coding exon hit with 2 or fewer mismatches? No. Exactly 1 bystander? No. → Not high.\n  - → low\n- g04: intergenic, 4 mismatches, low risk, 0 bystanders → low\n- g06: intergenic, 3 mismatches, low risk, 0 bystanders → low\n\nFor rejected guides:\n- g01:\n  - High-expression hit? Yes (expression_risk=high) → critical\n  - Also bystanders = 1, coding exon with 1 mismatch. But high expression alone → critical.\n- g03:\n  - High-expression hit? No (medium).\n  - Bystanders ≥ 2? No (0).\n  - Coding exon hit with 1 mismatch? No (2 mismatches).\n  - → Not critical. high? Coding exon hit with 2 or fewer mismatches? Yes (2 mismatches) → high.\n- g05:\n  - High-expression hit? Yes → critical.\n  - Also bystanders = 2 → critical (bystanders ≥ 2). Also coding exon with 1 mismatch → critical.\n\nTherefore:\n- g01: critical\n- g02: low\n- g03: high\n- g04: low\n- g05: critical\n- g06: low\n\n**Rule 3: Ranking**\n\nNon-rejected group: sort by descending activity_score, then by guide_id.\n- g02: 0.67\n- g04: 0.59\n- g06: 0.64\n\nDescending: g02 (0.67), g06 (0.64), g04 (0.59)\nRanks: g02=1, g06=2, g04=3\n\nRejected group: sort by high before critical, then descending activity_score, then guide_id.\n- g03: high, activity 0.74\n- g01: critical, activity 0.82\n- g05: critical, activity 0.78\n\nhigh first: g03 (high).\nNext critical: g01 (0.82), g05 (0.78). Descending activity: g01, g05.\nSo the rejected order: g03 (rank 4),